//! The four exponential tables `FastMath` ships as literals, as raw bit patterns.
//!
//! **Generated** from the oracle's own arrays; do not edit by hand. The conformance suite
//! `fastmath_exp` compares every entry against the golden, so a transcription error fails there.
//!
//! The port started by *computing* these with `FastMathCalc`, which is the reference's other
//! branch (`RECOMPUTE_TABLES_AT_RUNTIME`). The oracle was asked whether the two branches agree and
//! answered no: **577 of 5,050 entries differ**, all in the integer table. See
//! `docs/decisions/0024-fastmaths-two-table-branches-do-not-agree.md`. The branch that runs
//! upstream is the literals, so the literals are what the port carries.

